      "seed": 1214360697,
      "version": 1059,
      "versionNonce": 1717394748,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783718342227,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design interview: (RADIO)\n* Requirement exploration: understand the problem thoroughly and determine the scope by asking clarifying questions\n* Architecture/high level design: list out key components of products and how they relate to each other (always have high level design)\n* Data model/core entities: describe core entities and its data -- fields each entities contain/which component it belongs to\n* API: define API between component, functionality for each API, parameters and response\n* Optimization and deep-dive",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design interview: (RADIO)\n* Requirement exploration: understand the problem thoroughly and determine the scope by asking clarifying questions\n* Architecture/high level design: list out key components of products and how they relate to each other (always have high level design)\n* Data model/core entities: describe core entities and its data -- fields each entities contain/which component it belongs to\n* API: define API between component, functionality for each API, parameters and response\n* Optimization and deep-dive",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BfyAN-c9SGLwRQhmXc8ua",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410.3592425209106,
      "y": 309.38499579233354,
      "width": 638.4794921875,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "an",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1261772710,
      "version": 800,
      "versionNonce": 2144947076,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783723237889,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Fuzzy search: ***\n* handle typo in search, especially mobile device, use fuzzy search\nto match search query closely instead of exactly\n* Levenstain distance (find shortest distance) between\nsearch query and results\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Fuzzy search: ***\n* handle typo in search, especially mobile device, use fuzzy search\nto match search query closely instead of exactly\n* Levenstain distance (find shortest distance) between\nsearch query and results\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Wh3UKjTbq6sVg8CONMSE0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 339.98258337790594,
      "y": 1873.0214557928753,
      "width": 882.619384765625,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ar",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1298607354,
      "version": 1458,
      "versionNonce": 1592356412,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783723661146,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Accessibility\n* the combobox bulit from plain <input /> has no inherent semantic,\nso we need to lean on ARIA role and keyboard convention\nto make component usable in screenreader and keyboard\n* <ul>/<li> for list system with role=\"listbox\" or role=\"option\"\n* aria-label for input (if there is no visible label tag)\n* role=\"combobox\" for input tag\n* aria-haspopup to indicate the element can trigger an\ninteractive popup element\n* aria-expanded indicate whether the popup element is current displayed\n* aria-live (result region) so screen reader can be notified\n* aria-autocomplete to descirbe the type of autocompletion\ninteraction model\n(single line value -- autocomplete == 'inline'\ncollection value -- autocomplete == 'list')\n\n* User experience\n-- Autofocus\n-- Handle different state (loading, error, no network)\n-- Handle long string/long text with wrap or ellipsis. (no text overflow outside component)\n-- Mobile friendly (line height, each item can be large enough to tap in mobile device, \nresponse fit in mobile view port)\n-- Set helpful attributes for mobile: autocapitalize=\"off\", autocomplete=\"off\", \nautocorrect=\"off\", and spellcheck=\"false\" so that the browser suggestions \ndo not interfere with the user's search.\n-- Support keyboard interaction\n-- Where auto compleete response should appear (below/above), \ndepending on the position of the search bar\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Accessibility\n* the combobox bulit from plain <input /> has no inherent semantic,\nso we need to lean on ARIA role and keyboard convention\nto make component usable in screenreader and keyboard\n* <ul>/<li> for list system with role=\"listbox\" or role=\"option\"\n* aria-label for input (if there is no visible label tag)\n* role=\"combobox\" for input tag\n* aria-haspopup to indicate the element can trigger an\ninteractive popup element\n* aria-expanded indicate whether the popup element is current displayed\n* aria-live (result region) so screen reader can be notified\n* aria-autocomplete to descirbe the type of autocompletion\ninteraction model\n(single line value -- autocomplete == 'inline'\ncollection value -- autocomplete == 'list')\n\n* User experience\n-- Autofocus\n-- Handle different state (loading, error, no network)\n-- Handle long string/long text with wrap or ellipsis. (no text overflow outside component)\n-- Mobile friendly (line height, each item can be large enough to tap in mobile device, \nresponse fit in mobile view port)\n-- Set helpful attributes for mobile: autocapitalize=\"off\", autocomplete=\"off\", \nautocorrect=\"off\", and spellcheck=\"false\" so that the browser suggestions \ndo not interfere with the user's search.\n-- Support keyboard interaction\n-- Where auto compleete response should appear (below/above), \ndepending on the position of the search bar\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "spVvglj8D625mHmBkur_3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 348.3958380838501,
      "y": -488.73691924800687,
      "width": 894.9993286132812,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "at",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1676802362,
      "version": 396,
      "versionNonce": 1031656636,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783717498974,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Plug-and-Play Capability: The component should be sufficiently generalized to \nintegrate seamlessly into various environments or applications with minimal configuration.\n2. Customizable UI: Both the input field and search results UI must be customizable, \nallowing users to tailor the look and feel to match their application’s design.\n3. Data Source Versatility: The component must support both asynchronous data fetching \n(for API endpoints) and static data (client-side data), providing flexibility \nin how data is sourced and managed.\n   \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Plug-and-Play Capability: The component should be sufficiently generalized to \nintegrate seamlessly into various environments or applications with minimal configuration.\n2. Customizable UI: Both the input field and search results UI must be customizable, \nallowing users to tailor the look and feel to match their application’s design.\n3. Data Source Versatility: The component must support both asynchronous data fetching \n(for API endpoints) and static data (client-side data), providing flexibility \nin how data is sourced and managed.\n   \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
